    "page.connType.shadow.p.calculate-your-four-totem-animals-then": "Calculate your four totem animals, then browse the opt-in directory for people who share this connection type with you.",
    "page.connType.shadow.btn.totem-connections-directory": "Totem Connections Directory",
    "page.connType.shadow.btn.totem-animals-calculator": "Totem Animals Calculator",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.section-label.connection-type": "Connection Type",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.h1.mirror-opposite": "Mirror Opposite",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.p.opposites-on-the-zodiac-wheel-six": "Opposites on the zodiac wheel — six signs apart, facing each other directly across the circle. Ideal for reflecting blindspots and learning from a radically different point of view.",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.p.totem-connections": "<a href=\"connections.html?v=20260807\">← Totem Connections</a>",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.p.opposites-on-the-zodiac-wheel-six.2": "Opposites on the zodiac wheel — six signs apart, facing each other directly across the circle. These connections are perfect for reflecting ourselves and seeing each other's blindspots — as they are quite literally facing the opposite direction that you are! This can make for some heated arguments, but as long as you bring enough respect to the table, there's a lot to learn here from your mirrors — both of you can see things that the other cannot, so as long as you trust each other and act in good faith, this can be a very helpful and beautiful connection to have. It will most definitely keep things interesting, as they will no doubt have a different take on things than you, sometimes so radically different that you didn't even think it was possible!",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.h3.other-connection-types": "Other connection types",
    "page.connType.mirror-opposite.li.rainbow": "<a href=\"connection-rainbow.html?v=20260807\">Rainbow</a>",
